# 00 — Core Architecture

Applying Rules: [SEARCH_FIRST | NON_DESTRUCTIVE | STRICT_LOGIC | CORE]

Full contract: `GAME_MASTER_SPEC.md`. Source of record:
`docs/Military Game Design Plan.md`. This header is the short form every
session reads first.

## Response header

Begin every response with:

```
Applying Rules: [SEARCH_FIRST | NON_DESTRUCTIVE | STRICT_LOGIC | <ACTIVE_MODULE>]
```

`<ACTIVE_MODULE>` ∈ CORE, PROGRESSION, GUNSMITH, COMBAT, NARRATIVE, META, UI.

## Non-destructive rules

1. NEVER replace or delete working code. Extend it.
2. SEARCH FIRST — grep and semantic search before writing.
3. EXTEND, DO NOT MUTATE. Smallest possible diff; new types over edited ones.
4. PROTECT `MODULE_REGISTRY.json`. A `LOCKED_VERIFIED` module may not change its
   public API or core logic without explicit human override.
5. Keep every source file under 300 lines. No dead functions, no unused
   imports.
6. No hallucinated APIs — only rely on code that has been read.

## Six-step sequence

SCAN → PLAN → TEST CONTRACT → DOMAIN (`GameResult<T>`) → VIEW (EventBus) →
VERIFY (type check, lint, contract audit, logs).

## Where the code lives

| Spec module | Package |
| --- | --- |
| Core | `com.example.game.vanguard.core` |
| Progression | `com.example.game.vanguard.progression` |
| Gunsmith | `com.example.game.vanguard.gunsmith` |
| Combat | `com.example.game.vanguard.combat` |
| Narrative | `com.example.game.vanguard.narrative` |
| Meta | `com.example.game.vanguard.meta` |

Reuse `com.example.game.combat` geometry (`Vec3`, `BallisticBody`,
`BallisticsEngine`) rather than re-deriving it.

## Rule partitions

Keep each domain prompt scoped to one contract, so context does not drift:

- `00-core-architecture` — this file: header, golden rules, sequencing.
- `10-combat-ballistics` — six gates, hitboxes, stances, clearance.
- `20-gunsmith-crafting` — seven sockets, part specs, barrel swaps.
- `30-rank-narrative-fsm` — monotonic ranks, watchdog, dilemmas.
- `40-meta-persistence` — UTC production queues, governance, session flow.

## Verification

`VanguardContractAudit.audit()` runs every contract case in-process. A module is
only `LOCKED_VERIFIED` once that audit passes in full.
